.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T14:41:00Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T14:41:00Z","body":"That's the problem, there is no output of any kind, it just thinks and does nothing. I finally got an upgrade to work, after Copilot forced me to reboot after shutting it down, which has me wondering what Microsoft is running in the background and for what BS reason. But anyway, running newest build now so we shall see if it still sucks or if I will just give up and use ChatGPT. Either way I will report back after the weekend. Focusing on some Swift stuff in Xcode now to wash the bad taste out of my mouth.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2904664670/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2918613077","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10287#issuecomment-2918613077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10287","id":2918613077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6t9oBV","user":{"login":"PragmaticPraxis","id":6620400,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MjA0MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6620400?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis","html_url":"https://github.com/PragmaticPraxis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PragmaticPraxis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T07:51:39Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T07:51:39Z","body":"So, a perfect example here. Using Copilot inline, current version of VS Code Mac. Given this line\n`$sw = New-Object System.IO.StreamWriter($file)`\nWith either the cursor at the end of the line or highlighting the line, and the request \"Refactor this line to use a class method rather than New-Object\", Copilot thinks for a few seconds and then... stops thinking. No results, no message, no nothing. Useless.\n\nChat GPT, with an even more cryptic request gives me this.\n\nCan this line use a class method instead?\nChatGPT said:\nSure, I can help with that — but I need to see the line of code you're referring to. Could you share the specific line, and ideally the class it belongs to? That way, I can tell whether it can or should be converted to a class method.\n\nYou said:\n$sw = New-Object System.IO.StreamWriter($file)\nChatGPT said:\nYes, the line:\n\n$sw = New-Object System.IO.StreamWriter($file)\ncan be replaced with a class method — specifically, you can use the static .CreateText() method of the [System.IO.File] class, which returns a StreamWriter. Here's how:\n\nAlternative using a class method:\n$sw = [System.IO.File]::CreateText($file)\nExplanation:\n[System.IO.File]::CreateText($file) is a static method that creates or overwrites a file and returns a StreamWriter.\nThis approach is cleaner and more idiomatic in PowerShell when using .NET classes.\nImportant:\nBoth approaches return a StreamWriter, so behavior will be similar.\nJust like with New-Object, you still need to call $sw.Close() or wrap it in a try/finally block or use using if you're on PowerShell 5+.\nWould you like a version that auto-disposes the writer as well?\n\nPretty damn embarrassing, don't you think. Copilot USED to give me valid answers, but for maybe the last month I get this Trump level uselessness probably 70% of the time, and when I do get results it's still frustrating because a request to refactor results in added code not replaced code, and errors as a result that I have to fix manually. \n\nIt's bad enough I am uninstalling. I'm just glad it happened before I started paying, because paying for this typical Microsoft garbage would have really pissed me off.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2918613077/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3648080726","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10287#issuecomment-3648080726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10287","id":3648080726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc7ZcUtW","user":{"login":"rzhao271","id":7199958,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTk5NTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7199958?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rzhao271","html_url":"https://github.com/rzhao271","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rzhao271/followers","following_url":"https://ap